            <ArticleTitle>Sudden bilateral reversible vision loss: a rare presentation of acute intermittent porphyria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>432-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute intermittent porphyria is a rare disorder, characterised clinically by variable patterns of neurological and metabolic disturbances. We report a rare presentation with sudden onset painless bilateral reversible vision loss of cerebral origin along with a brief review of the underlying pathophysiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
